# "When another creature you control leaves the battlefield": control, not ownership. On turn 3 Bot1's Dack Fayden takes
# Bot2's Ornithopter (−2: gain control of target artifact), and Bot1 exiles it with Swords to Plowshares. It was a creature
# Bot1 controlled as it left, though Bot2 owns it, so Aang triggers, and at the next upkeep (Bot2's, turn 4) he transforms
# into Aang, Destined Savior. Bot2's Ornithopter leaving under Bot2's control does not trigger him
# (`aang-at-the-crossroads-ignores-an-opponents-creature-and-a-noncreature-leaving`).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Aang, at the Crossroads
Mox Ruby
Dack Fayden
Island x5
Swords to Plowshares
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Aang, at the Crossroads.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Dack Fayden.Activate(Ability: Gain control; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Aang, at the Crossroads.Power = 3
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Aang, Destined Savior.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby; Dack Fayden; Aang, Destined Savior
